\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  36\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (Pseudo-){\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Augustinus Dati}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Elegantiolae}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  cum appendices et glossis, unvollst\u228 \'e4ndig. (3\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Credimus iam dudum a plerisque viris etiam disertissimis}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (33\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Conclusio opusculi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Non igitur plura scribens\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 exercutacioni accomoda\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Nachtrag: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Vale\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Nachgetragene Rubrik: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Augustini Dati Senensis oratoris primari Isagogicus libellus in elocutionis precepta explicitus est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . De oratione regulae tredecim. Text: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Pro maiori autem exercitacione nanciscenda preceptorum summulam una cum orandi modo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 collacionem spectat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Rubrik: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Regula prima\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Text: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sepe sese augeat oratio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (35\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 a summis poetis atque oratoribus sunt recepta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Peter Luder}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (?), Modus orandi. >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Modus orandi ita et primum de genere peticionis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Peticionis loci sunt quatuor\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... Text bricht ab: (36\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Aliud genus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Que dicta sunt de genere peticionis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 si non comodum suum attendere nostre saltem benevolencie causa id facere velit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Text bricht aufgrund von Blattverlust ab; 2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Wiederholung des Textanfangs (Credimus iam dudum ... nascetur exordium) mit Glosse zu \u8218 \'82etiam dissertissimis persuasum\lquote ; Druck: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 GW 08032, 08037, 08038, 08042, 08047, 08049, 08070, 08073, 08109, 08123 \endash  08137}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (08123 \endash  08133: mit Peter Luder, Modus orandi); vgl. Bertalot, Initia, 1985 \endash  2004, Bd. 2,1, (1990), S. 150, Nr. 2771; Bd. 2,2 (2004), S. 871, Nr. 15547; S. 1294, Nr. 22627; Bursill-Hall, Census, 1981, S. 306; Jacqueline Hamesse/ Slawomir Szyler (Hrsg.), Repertorium initiorum manuscriptorum Latinorum Medii Aevi, 4 B\u228 \'e4nde, Louvain-la-Neuve 2007 \endash  2010, Bd. 1 (2007), S. 542, Nr. 9027; C.A.L.M.A., Bd. 1,4 (2001), S. 498 \endash  502 (Elisabetta Guerrieri), bes. Nr. 17, Polak, Letter Treatises, 1993 \endash  2015, (2015), S. 371, S. 19; zu dem Modus orandi des Peter Luder vgl. Frank E. Baron, The Beginnings of German Humanism. The Life and Work of Wandering Peter Luder, Diss. Ann Arbor/ Michigan 1966, S. 124 und 196; Eske Bockelmann, Die Metrikvorlesung des Fr\u252 \'fchhumanisten Peter Luder, Bamberg 1984 (Gratia. Bamberger Schriften zur Renaissanceforschung, H. 14), S. 162, Nr. I.3; VL(2), Bd. 5 (1985), Sp. 954 \endash  959 (Frank Baron), bes. Sp. 957; 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa360\itap0 (3\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Glosse beginnt: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Presentis opusculi talis prescribitur titulus Augustini Daci Senensis literas pro conficiendis epistolis ad Andream ducem Cristofferi filius libellus incipit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 foeliciter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 In hoc titulo non auctoris ac libri commoventi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... marginal: \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dudum et iam dudum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \lquote  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 dicit per nove\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (?) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 tempore unius hore aut semi hore ad duarum horarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (27\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Glosse endet: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Habeo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Habeo variam constructionem figuratum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Negotia mea\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 bene se habent atque\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 optatem consuetudine meis sum contenta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \endash  Marginale und interlineare Glossen; enden unvermittelt weit vor dem Schlu\u223 \'df des Textes. }

