\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  52\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Marcus Tullius Cicero}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 De Oratore}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , Fragment. Anfang fehlt; Text beginnt: 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  mit Buch 1, 16, 69: <quid est cur non orator de rebus iis eloquentissime> \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 dicat, quas ad certam causam tempusque cognorit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ? \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Est finitimus oratori poeta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (4\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (1, 22, 99): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 neque quo tuo studio rectissimo atque optimo non ob\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u9553 \'a6<sequi vellem>; (5\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (1, 31, 137): <non negabo me>\u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ista omnium communia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [et] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 contrita praecepta didicisse\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (6\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (1, 34, 155): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 si eciam exprimerem quaedam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6<verba imitando>; (7\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (1, 44, 197): <de quo>\u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 multa soleo in sermonibus quotidianis dicere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (8\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (1, 48, 210): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Nam si forte quaereretur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6 <quae esset ars imperatoris>; (9\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (1, 17, 244): <quid in illa causa, cum contra te>\u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 diceret\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ut tulit quod de iure civili depromptum videretur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (10\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (1, 60, 24): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Quod si ille\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \u9553 \'a6<adstrictus certa quadam numerorum moderatione et pedum>; (11\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 2, 5): <sed ne sine omni quidem sapientia florere umquam> \u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et praestare potuisse\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (11\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 3, 11): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 omissa omni adhortacione ad eorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6 <quos proposuimus sermonem disputationemque veniamus>; (12\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 4, 17): <vel dignitatis vel commodi rationem>\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \u9553 \'a6 non habet aut denique in aliquo genere aut inconcinnus aut multus est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (12\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 6, 24): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod tu scripseris, omnes ad\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 te\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6 <cives cum tabulis veniemus>; (13\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 9, 37): <aut cum aliqua> \u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 alia arte esse commune\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (13\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 10, 43): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 eciamsi opus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6<est, minus est tamen necessarium>; (14\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 12, 50): <quae in lite dicuntur, obiur->\u9553 \'a6\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 gatio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 consolacio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quorum nihil est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (17\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 18, 74): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 neque enim aetas id mea desiderat et aliud quoddam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6<dicendi nos secuti sumus>; (18\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 20, 87): <qui erit talis ut cohortan->\u9553 \'a6\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 dus adiuvandusque sit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (28\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 38, 158): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et adiuncta sint alia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 iudicent\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6 <rectene adiuncta sint>; (29\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 41, 174): <de quo genere toto pau->\u9553 \'a6\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 lo dixi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Haec ut brevissime dici potuerunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (32\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 47, 197): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ut ego ad id re\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 -\u9553 \'a6<stinguendum vix conarer accedere>; (33\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 51, 207): <quam> \u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 defendas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  aut diginitatem inesse\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (33\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 53, 212): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ad hanc vim acerrimam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 qua eosdem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (!) \u9553 \'a6 <excitamus>; (34\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 54, 219): <verum tamen> \u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ut dicis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Antoni\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (37\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 59, 242): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 hoc ipso genere ridiculum ut cau\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 -\u9553 \'a6<tissime tractandum sit>; (38\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 61, 249): <nec obsignatum nec> \u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 occlusum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (!), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod idem in bono servo dici solet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (38\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 63, 255): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quae genera percurram equidem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6<sed scitis esse notissimum ridiculi genus>; (39\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 64, 260): <ridicule illud etiam L.> \u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Portius Nascia censori Catoni\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (44\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 74, 299): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sed ego non\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6 <de praestanti>; (45\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 75, 305): <sed quia causam non libenter relinquo> \u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 nimium patiens et lentus existimor\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (47\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 80, 328): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod gestum esse dicas cum etiam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6 <quem ad modum actum sit exponas>; (48\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 84, 341): <et quod nos> \u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 laudationibus non ita multum uti soleremus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (50\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (2, 88, 359): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quae\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quasi articuli connectunt membra orationis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quae for\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 -\u9553 \'a6<mari similitudine nulla possunt>; (51\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (2, 89, 364): <Crasso dicente nemo tam adrogans, qui> \u9553 \'a6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 similiter se unquam dicturum esse consideret\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (51\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab: (2, 90, 367): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quam primum tamen audire velle dixerunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \u9553 \'a6 <(3, 1, 1) Instituenti mihi, Quinte frater>; (52\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt (3, 6, 24): <non suscipiam oratione mea plus quam mihi im->\u9553 \'a6\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ponitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tantum significabo brevi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (52\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text bricht ab (3, 8, 31): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et quid iudici probandum sit cum acutissime vidit, omissis ceteris \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u9553 \'a6<argumentis in eo mentem orationemque defigit>. \endash  Anfang und Schlu\u223 \'df fehlen; Text bricht aufgrund von Blattverlusten mehrfach ab; enthalten sind mit Unterbrechungen Buch 1, 16, 69 \endash  Buch 3, 8, 31; zum Textbestand im einzelnen s.o.; Druck: Kazmierz F. Kumaniecki (Hrsg.), M. Tulli Ciceronis Scripta quae manserunt omnia. Fasc. 3: De oratore, Stuttgart/ Leipzig \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1969 (Reprint 1995) (Bibliotheca Scriptorum Graecorum et Romanorum Teubneriana), S. 28 \endash  274; Augustus S. Wilkins (Hrsg.), M. Tulli Ciceronis De Oratore Libri Tres, Oxford 1892 (Reprint: Amsterdam 1962); vgl. Munk Olsen, \u201 \'c9tude, 1982 \endash  1989, Bd. 1 (1982), S. 109, S. 126, Nr. #401 \endash  #402. }

