\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 19\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  22\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Leonardo Bruni}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (?), {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Novella di Seleuco e Antioco}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (19\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Novella bellissima et legiadra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\strike\lang1033\fs26 Tra\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  di Seleuco\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  re di Soria\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  et d\rquote Antioco\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  suo figliuolo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tracta dell\rquote antiche hystorie et in volgare ydioma per lo excellentissimo oratore Leonardo Aretino composta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Contraria ad quella di Tancredi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666v/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Non sono molti anni passati, che trovando mi in compagnia}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  di piu gentili huomini et donne\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (19\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ad me e sempre paruto\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dovete adunque sapere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (22\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et se medesimo d\rquote ogni contentamento per ruvidezza di natura privare in perpetuo sostenne\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Finita\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: Marcelli, Novella, 2003 (s. Lit.), S. 7 \endash  174; bes. S. 145 \endash  174 vgl. ebenda, S. 50 \endash  51 u.\u246 \'f6., Sigle D; Vittore Branca, Tradizione delle opere di Giovanni Boccaccio, 2 B\u228 \'e4nde, Rom 1958 und 1991 (Edizioni di Storia e Letteratura Bd. 66 und 175), Bd. 1, S. 75 \endash  76, Bd. 2, S. 17; vgl. Baron, Leonardo Bruni Aretino, 1928/ 1969, S. 176; Hankins, Repertorium Brunianum, 1997, S. 30, Nr. 344; Berti, Cicerone, 2010, S. 59 (s. Lit.). }

