\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  106\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Eberhardus Bethuniensis}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Graecismus}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  cum Glossa, Fragment. Text beginnt: (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Rubrik: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De masculinis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Text: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Est pater hic cura, pater est alius genitura}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (101\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Rubrik (nachgetragen auf dem Kopfsteg): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De verbis mixtis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Text: (N)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 arro refert signat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 hoc pertinet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 hoc quoque distat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... Text endet: (106\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ista sed excipias et que componis ab illis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Con. dis. cog. glis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 pos. in fus. co. no. qui as. cres. pas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Glosse beginnt marginal. (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Finito primo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  <...> \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 in quo agit auctor de Grecis dictionibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 aggreditur secundum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  in quo agit de dictionibus Latiniis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dividitur autem liber iste primo in duas partes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  in quarum prima agit de nomine\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  in secunda de pronomine\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... Glosse endet marginal (106\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Pasco Pascis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 dare pastum ponitur eciam quinque pro desciscere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  ut ovis pavit pratum id est depavit et corroscit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Der Text beginnt mit Kapitel 9 und endet mit Kapitel 19; mit marginalen und interlinearen Glossen; Druck (Text): Wrobel, Grecismus, 1887, S. 54 \endash  187; vgl. Glorieux, Facult\u233 \'e9, Nr. 97; Bursill-Hall, Census, 1981, Nr. 69.1; LMA, Bd. 3 (1986), S. 1523 (U. Kindermann); Weijers, Travail, 1994ff., Bd. 3,2 (1996), S. 58 \endash  59; C.A.L.M.A., Bd. 3 (2011), S. 169 (R. Forrai); zur Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Bursill-Hall, Teaching Grammars, 1977, S. 1 \endash  29, bes. S. 12 \endash  14; Grondeux, Graecismus, 1990 \endash  1991, S. 71 \endash  101; Grondeux, Gloses, 2000; Text auch in {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5007[0].501m/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Hs 15}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , 340\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5007[0].501m/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Hs 20}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5007[0].501m/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Hs 2508}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r}

