\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  91\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Galfredus de Vino Salvo}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Poetria nova}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  cum commentario {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Nicolai de Dybin}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (magistri Tibini Pragensis). (6\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Papa stupor mundi si duxero papa Nocenti}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (91\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text endet unvermittelt: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Quando venit suspensa nimes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (statt: nimis) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 constructio longa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 addiciunt sextam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quando traiectio verbi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 inconsina venit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ut\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Lucil misuus elli\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (statt: Luci lusimus Elyn). (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Kommentar beginnt: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Omnia subiecisti subiecisti sub pedibus eius oves et boves\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (Ps 8, 7). {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Verba proposita scripta sunt per prophetam in Psalmo dignicantibus}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Papa stupor\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tulius primo Rethorice sue describit Rethoricam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 dicens\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Rethorica est scientia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 docens de quocumque perswasibili decenter invenire materias\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (91\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et viciorum exstirpacione et dividitur in sex\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 partes et tamen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod docet exstirpare\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  sex vicia partes patent in processu\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hic est unde primum vicium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quid tangitur hic\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Text und Kommentar brechen unver\-mittelt in Abschnitt IV.5, Vers 1942 der Ausgabe von Faral (s.u.) ab; Druck (Text): Edmond Faral (Hrsg.), Les arts po\u233 \'e9tiques du xii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 e\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  et du xiii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 e\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  si\u232 \'e8cle. Recherches et documents sur la technique litter\u233 \'e9raire du Moyen \u194 \'c2ge, Paris 1958, S. 197 \endash  257; Ernest Gallo, The \u8218 \'82Poetria Nova\lquote  and its Sources in Early Rhetorical Doctrine, Den Haag/ Paris 1971 (De proprietatibus litterarum, Series Maior, Bd. 10), S. 14 \endash  118 (Vers 1947); vgl. Glorieux, Facult\u233 \'e9, Nr. 112c.; {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Walther, Versanf\u228 \'e4nge, Nr. 16656}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; Weijers, Travail, 1994ff., Bd. 3 (1998), S. 66 \endash  69, bes. S. 68; C.A.L.M.A., Bd. 4 (2014), S. 129 \endash  133 ( J.-Y. Tiliette); zum Kommentator vgl. Hans Szklenar, Magister Nicolaus de Dybin. Vorstudien zu einer Edition seiner Schriften: Ein Beitrag zur Geschichte der literarischen Rhetorik im sp\u228 \'e4teren Mittelalter, M\u252 \'fcnchen 1981 (MTU, Bd. 65), bes. S. 100 \endash  110, 158 \endash  160, 292 \endash  293; VL (2), Bd. 6 (1987), Sp. 1062 \endash  1068 (Hans Szklenar), bes. Sp. 1065, Nr. 2; Marjorie Curry Woods, Classroom Com\-mentaries. Teaching the \u8218 \'82Poetria Nova\lquote  Across Medieval and Renaissance Europe, Columbus 2010 (Text and Context), S. 182 \endash  209, 289 \endash  307 (Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung ohne diese Hs.), 317, 318. \endash  92\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  99\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  leer. }

