\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 166\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  181\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (Pseudo-){\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Claudius Ptolemaeus}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Centiloquium}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (Translatio {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Platonis Tiburtini}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) cum commento {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[2].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\fs26\chcbpat17 Abu-'l-\u7716 ?asan \u703 ?Al\u299 \'ee Ibn-Ab\u299 \'ee-'r-Ri\u487 ?\u257 \'e2l}}\plain \f2\fs26  (Haly). (166\plain \f2\super\fs24 ra\plain \f2\fs26 ) Text beginnt: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\i\fs26\chcbpat17 Dixit Ptolomeus: Iam scripsi tibi iesure libros}}\plain \f2\fs26  ... \plain \f2\i\fs26 Sciencia stellarum ex te et illis est astrologus\plain \f2\fs26  ... (181\plain \f2\super\fs24 rb\plain \f2\fs26 ) Text endet: \plain \f2\i\fs26 erit proditor ex aliqua civitatum illius climatis\plain \f2\fs26 . (166\plain \f2\super\fs24 ra\plain \f2\fs26 ) Kommentar beginnt: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\i\fs26\chcbpat17 Haly}}\plain \f2\fs26\chcbpat17 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\i\fs26\chcbpat17 Quod dixit Ptolomeus ex te et illis significat}}\plain \f2\fs26 , \plain \f2\i\fs26 quod qui res futuras\plain \f2\fs26  ... (181\plain \f2\super\fs24 va\plain \f2\fs26 ) Kommentar endet: \plain \f2\i\fs26 perfecta est huius libri translatio 17 die mensis Marcii 12. die mensis Mymedi secundi anno Arabum \plain \f2\i\strike\fs26 tricessimo\plain \f2\i\fs26  309 Ar. 530\plain \f2\fs26 . (166\plain \f2\super\fs24 rab\plain \f2\fs26 ) Marginale Glosse beginnt: \u8218 \'82\plain \f2\i\fs26 Dixit Ptolemeus\plain \f2\fs26 : \plain \f2\i\fs26 Jesure\plain \f2\fs26 \lquote  \plain \f2\i\fs26 nomen proprium viri\plain \f2\fs26  \u8218 \'82\plain \f2\i\fs26 libros\plain \f2\fs26 \lquote  \plain \f2\i\fs26 scilicet quadripartitum\plain \f2\fs26  ... (173\plain \f2\super\fs24 rab\plain \f2\fs26 ) Fu\u223 \'dfsteg Schlu\u223 \'df beschnitten, letztes sinnvoll lesbares Satzfragment der marginalen Glosse (zum Abschnitt \u252 \'fcber die Coniunctiones): \plain \f2\i\fs26 et pro prophetas approbata si bene ista lex mundum ven\plain \f2\fs26 \u9553 ? <...>. \endash  Die Verfasserschaft der \u220 \'dcbersetzung wird in der neueren Forschung dem {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\fs26\chcbpat17 Plato Tiburtinus}}\plain \f2\fs26  zugeschrieben; Druck: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\fs26\chcbpat17 GW M36394}}\plain \f2\fs26 ; vgl. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[1].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\fs26\chcbpat17 Thorndike/ Kibre 1963, Sp. 1401}}\plain \f2\fs26 ; Carmody, Latin Translation, 1956 (s.o. 153\plain \f2\super\fs24 ra\plain \f2\fs26 ), S. 16, Nr. 3b; Maureen Robinson, The Heritage of Medieval Errors in The Latin Manuscripts of Johannes Hispalensis (Johan of Seville), in: Al-Qantara. Revista de etudios \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u225 \'e1rabes 28 (2007), S. 41 \endash  71, bes. S. 54; Jean- Patrice Boudet, Astrology between Rational Science and Divine Inspiration. The Pseudo-Ptolemy\rquote s Centiloquium, in: Stefano Rapisarda/ Erik Niblaeus (Hrsg.), Dialogues among Books in Medieval Western Magic and Divination, Florenz 2014 (Micrologus\rquote  Library, Bd. 65), S. 49 \endash  75, bes. 51 \endash  52; Dag Nikolaus Hasse, Stylistic Evidence for Identifying John of Seville with the Translator of Some Twelfth-Century Astrological and Astronomical Texts from Arabic into Latin on the Iberian Peninsula, in: C. Burnett/\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 P. Mantas-Espa\u241 \'f1a (Hrsg.):\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Ex Oriente Lux. Translating Words, Scripts and Styles in Medieval Mediterranean Society, C\u243 \'f3rdoba/ London 2016, S. 19 \endash  43; Juste, \u8218 \'82MS Darmstadt, Hessische Landes- und Hochschulbibliothek, 739\rquote  (s. Lit.); David Juste, Work B.1.2. \u8218 \'82Pseudo-Ptolemy, Centiloquium (tr. Plato of Tivoli)\rquote , in: Internet-Projekt der Bayerischen Akademie der Wissenschaften, Ptolemaeus Arabus et Latinus. Works, online unter: http://ptolemaeus.badw.de/work/41 (update:21.05.2020). }

