\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 253\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  253\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [250\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  250\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ] {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Averroes}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 De substantia orbis}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  cum commentario {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Johannis de Ianduno}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , Fragment. (253\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text beginnt: >Ulterius notandum est, quod sicut rarum et densum ... quod hoc lumen fit ex commixtione rari cum denso>\u9553 \'a6{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 in celo vero non sed per suam naturam}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  simplicem et luminosum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (253\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text endet: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sed ista dispositio in eis etc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Primo quia dixerat statim\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod necesse est de venire ad alterans non alteratum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u9553 \'a6 <subditur modo differentiam inter alterationem et motum localem ...>. \endash  Fragment aus Kapitel 2; Druck: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 GW 2336 \endash  2339, 2427}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; vgl. Glorieux, Facult\u233 \'e9; Nr. 242d.); Lacombe, Aristoteles Latinus, 1955 \endash  1957, Bd. 1, S. 111 und 233; Weijers, Travail, 1994ff., Bd. 11,5 (2003), S. 87 \endash  104, bes. S. 94; Dag Nikolaus Hasse, Latin Averroes Translations of the First Half of the Thirteenth Century (Plenary Session Paper Read on 21 September 2007 in Palermo at the XII International Congress of Medieval Philosophy), Hildesheim/ Z\u252 \'fcrich/ New York 2010.}

