\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 145\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  147\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (Pseudo-){\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Beda Venerabilis}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Prognostica temporum}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (Bearb.). (145\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Nachtrag: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Prima dies sunt Kalende Januarii etc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Text: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Januarii: Si in Dominica evenerit hiemps bona erit}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  et estas ventuosa vindemia bona boves crescunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; (147\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Si in sexta feria fuerit hyemps inutilis est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Si in Sabbato fuerit hyemps turbinosa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (147\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 erit ipso anno non ventuosa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 infirmus diu languescet et vix evadet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 etc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Die Handschrift enth\u228 \'e4lt nur den ersten Abschnitt des Beda Venerabilis zugeschriebenen Textes; diesen jedoch in einer erweiternden Bearbeitung; Druck: PL, Bd. 90, Sp. 951; vgl. Charles W. Jones, Bedae Pseudepigrapha. Scientific Writings Falsely Attributed to Bede, Ithaca/ London/ Oxford 1939, S. 87; {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Thorndike/ Kibre 1963, Sp. 1457; Sp. 1449, 11 \endash  12}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; L\u225 \'e1szl\u243 \'f3 S\u225 \'e1ndor Cardonnens, Anglo-Saxon Prognostics 900 \endash  1100. Study and Texts, Leiden/ Boston 2007 (Brill\rquote s Studies in Intellectual History, Bd. 153; Brill\rquote s Texts and Sources in Intellectual History, Bd. 3), S. 491 \endash  500.}

