\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 88\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 +r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ] \endash  196\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [109\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 +r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ] {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Picatrix}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (88\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) [1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 +r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ] >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit opus dignissimum sapientissimi Picatricis philosophi Arabici maximi in scientia mathematicorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Prohemium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Ad laudem gloriam et honorem altissimi et omnipotentis dei}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cuius est revelare suis predestinatis secreta scientiarum et ad illustrationem etiam doctorum Latinorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quibus est inopia librorum ab antiquis philosophis editorum Alphonsus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 dei gracia rex Hispanie illustrissimus totiusque Bandalusie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 precepit hunc librum summo studio summaque diligentia de Arabico in Hispanicum transferri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cuius nomen est Picatrix\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hoc autem opus perfectum fuit anno domini millesimo ducentesimo Alexandri M\u176 \'b0 D\u176 \'b0 lxviii\u176 \'b0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 1508\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cesaris vero m\u176 \'b0 cc\u176 \'b0 lxxxv\u176 \'b0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 1285\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Arabum D\u176 \'b0C\u176 \'b0lv\u176 \'b0 >655<\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quem ex ducentis et pluribus libris philosophie \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (?) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 compilavit et suo proprio nomine nominavit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Prohemium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit in nomine domini liber\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quem sapientissimus philosophus Picatrix in nigromanticis artibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ex quam pluribus libris philosophorum Arabum et aliarum nationum compilavit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et sapiens ait\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Primum quod agere debemus in omnibus rebus mundi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  est deo regratiari \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (88\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) [1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 +v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ] Kapitelverzeichnis. \u8230 \'85 Kapitel 1: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Capitulum primum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Cognoscendi in quo gradu es\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Scias\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 frater carissime\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod maius donum et nobilius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod deus hominibus huius mundi dederit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 est scire \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (195\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) [108\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 +v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 omnia vero\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 qui ad gloriam et honorem et altitudinem aquirendum fiunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 debes scribere super ipsius imaginis caput\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et sic finitur opus sapientissimi Picatricis philosophi \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Finis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Unmittelbar anschlie\u223 \'dfend\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 : >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Nota\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Opus magnum ad amoren scilicet sapienter nota\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Quermiex\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 tes \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (?), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 nerus quemis dius \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (196\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) [109\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 +r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Leyequin\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leyelgane\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leyequit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leyeguerich, leyerit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leierus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leycris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hec nomina scribe in manica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quam combures et dum comburitur legas nomina supradicta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et ex hoc amor et amicitia movebuntur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et sic finitur liber sapientis Picatricis in mathematicis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Finis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Verfasserzuweisung umstritten; Druck/ vgl: Hellmut Ritter (Hrsg.), \plain \f2\fs26 Kit\u257 \'e2b \u288 ?\u257 \'e2yat al-\u7717 ?ak\u299 \'eem wa-a\u7717 ?aqq an-nat\u299 \'ee\u487 ?atain bi-\u702 ?t-taqd\u299 \'eem, Leipzig/ Berlin\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  1933 (Studien der Bibliothek Warburg, Bd. 12); ders., Picatrix, ein arabisches Handbuch hellenistischer Magie, in: Vortr\u228 \'e4ge der Bibliothek Warburg 1 (1922), S. 94 \endash  124; vgl. Hellmut Ritter/ Martin Plessner (Hrsg.), Picatrix. Das Ziel des Weisen von Pseudo-Mar\plain \f3\lang1055\fs26 \u287 \'f0\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 r\plain \f2\fs26 \u299 \'ee\u7789 ?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 i. Translated into German From The Arabic by Hellmut Ritter and Martin Plessner,  London 1962 (Studies of the Warburg Institute, Bd. 27); \plain \f2\fs26 David Pingree, Picatrix: The Latin Version of the \u288 ?\u257 \'e2yat al-\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u7717 ?\plain \f2\fs26 ak\u299 \'eem, London 1986 (\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Studies of the Warburg Institute, Bd. 39), S. xii \endash  xv, xx \endash  lvii; Jean-Patrice Boudet/ Jean Charles Coulon, La version A\plain \f2\fs26 rabe (Gh\u257 \'e2yat al-\u7717 ?ak\u299 \'eem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) et la version Latine du Picatrix. Points communs et divergences, in: Jean-Patrice-Boudet/ Isabelle Draelants (Hrsg.), Textes et savoirs scientifiques et magiques m\u233 \'e9di\u233 \'e9vaux entre Orient et Occident, Paris 2017 (CRMH. Cahiers de recherches m\u233 \'e9di\u233 \'e9vales et humanistes. A Journal of Medieval and Humanistic Studies 33 (2017)), S. 67 \endash  101; vgl. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Thorndike/ Kibre 1963, Sp. 52}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; Thorndike, History, 1923 \endash  1958, Bd. 2 (1923), S. 813 \endash  824; Reimund Leicht, Astrologumena Judaica, Untersuchungen zur Geschichte der astrologischen Literatur der Juden, T\u252 \'fcbingen 2006 (Texts and Studies in Medieval and Early Modern Judaism, Bd. 21), S. 316 \endash  320; Text auch in {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5007[0].501m/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Hs 362}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . }

