\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ciii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  cviii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Visio Philiberti}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (Fulberti) sive Dialogus inter corpus et animam. (ciii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Noctis sub silencio tempore brumali dedicusque amodo sopreno spumali}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (cviii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 rebus transitoriis ab re nuntiavi et me Christi manibus totum commendavi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit lis de corpore et de anima\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. Anschlie\u223 \'dfend um 90\u176 \'b0 gedreht zur Schriftspalte Besitzvermerk des 17. Jhs. (s.o. Geschichte). \endash  Text ohne Glossierung und interlineare Zahlglossen; Druck: Ed\u233 \'e9lestand Du Meril, Po\u233 \'e9sies populaires latines ant\u233 \'e9rieures au douzi\u232 \'e8me si\u232 \'e8cle, Paris 1843, S. 219 \endash  230; Thomas Wright, The Latin Poems Commonly Attributed to Walter Mapes, London 1841 (Reprint Hildesheim 1968), S. 95 \endash  106 und 149 \endash  150; vgl. Walther, Streitgedicht, 1920/ 1984, S. 63 \endash  74, 211 \endash  214; {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 ders., Versanf\u228 \'e4nge, Nr. 11894}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; Rosemary Woolf, The English Religious Lyric in the Middle Ages, Oxford 1968, S. 90 \endash  91, 94, 326 \endash  328, 365, 369; {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[1].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Bloomfield/ Guyot, Incipits, Nr. 3223}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; Newhauser/ Bejczy, Bloomfield, 2008; Nr. 3223; VL(2), Bd. 10 (1999), Sp. 412 \endash  418 (Nigel F. Palmer); Neil Cartlidge, In the Silence of a Midwinter Night: A Re-Evaluation of the Visio Philiberti, in: Medium aevum 75 (2006), S. 24 \endash  45; Orb\u225 \'e1n, Novus Phisiologus, 1989 (s. Lit.), S. 10; Kohush\u246 \'f6lter, Gregorius, 2012 (s. Lit.), S. 55; Rubel, S\u252 \'fcnder, \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 2009 /\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 2019 (s. Lit.), S. 40; zur Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung jetzt: David P. Baker/ Neil Cartlidge, Manuscripts of the Medieval Latin Debate Between Body and Soul (Visio Philiberti), in: Notes and Queries 61.2 (2014), S. 196 \endash  201, bes. S. 198, Nr. 40; Text auch in {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5007[0].501m/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Hs 2272}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , 47\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; vgl. DA ULB Kat. 5,2. }

