\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  261\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Picatrix}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ({\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 A)}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 d laudem et gloriam altissimi omnipotentis dei}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cuius est revelare suis secretissematis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (!)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  scientie et ad illustracionem doctorum Latinorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quibus est inopia librorum ab antiquis philozophis editorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Alfuncius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 illustrissimus rex Hispaniorum tociusque Hadachye\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 precepit hunc librum summo studio summaque diligencia de Arabia in Hispanicum transferri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cuius nomen est Picatris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hoc autem perfectum sit anno domini M vel \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (?)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  vi Allexandri M D lxviii\u176 \'b0 cesaris m et lxxxxv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Et Iorabicum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (!)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  DC LV sapiens enim philosophus nobilis et honoratus Picatris hunc librum ex 200\u176 \'b0 libris et pluribus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [libris]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  philosophie compilavit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  quem suo proprio nomine nominavit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Prohemium: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 In nomine domini incipit liber\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  quem sapientissimus philosophus Picatris in nigromanticis artibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ex quam pluribus composuit. Et sapiens ayt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 :\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Primum quod agere debemus in omnibus rebus mundi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  est deo regraciari \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 )\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat7  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Kapitel 1, Rubrik: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Capitulum primum. De Sciencia cognoscendi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  in quo gradu es\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Text: (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 S\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 )\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cias\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 o\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 frater karissime\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod maius donum et nobilius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod deus hominibus huius mundi dederit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 est scire \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (261\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 omnia vero\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 que ad gloriam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  honorem et altitudinem acquirendum fiunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 debes scribere super frontem ipsius ymaginis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et sic finitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Anschlie\u223 \'dfend: (Q)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 uermiex\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 tos\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 herus quemis drinus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (261\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 )\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Leyequin\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 yelgane\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leyrquir\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leyrguerich, leyerit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leyerus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leyexeris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hec nomina scribe in manica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quam comburas et dum comburitur legas nomina supradicta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et ex hoc amor et amicicia movebuntur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et sic finitur sapiens Picatris in mathematicis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Deo gracias. Laus deo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  pax vivis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 requiem eternam defunctis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Anno domini 1509\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 9. Mey completus est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Verfasserzuweisung umstritten; Druck und vgl.\plain \f2\fs26 : Hellmut Ritter (Hrsg.), \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Kit\u257 ab \u288 G\u257 ayat al-\u7717 ?ak\u299 im wa-a\u7717 ?aqq an-nat\u299 i\u487 gatain bi-\u702 ?t-taqd\u299 im\plain \f2\fs26 , Leipzig/ Berlin 1933 (Studien der Bibliothek Warburg, Bd. 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 );\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Perrone Compagni, Picatrix, 1975, S. 281 und S. 286 \endash  337; Hellmut Ritter, Picatrix, ein arabisches Handbuch hellenistischer Magie, in: Vortr\u228 \'e4ge der Bibliothek Warburg 1 (1922), S. 94 \endash  124; vgl. ders.\plain \f3\lang1055\fs26 / Martin Plessner (Hrsg.), Picatrix. Das Ziel des Weisen von Pseudo-Mar\u287 \'f0r\plain \f2\fs26 \u299 \'ee\u7789 ?i. Translated \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 into German From t\plain \f2\fs26 he Arabic by Hellmut Ritter and Martin Plessner, London 1962 (Studies of the Warburg Institute, Bd. 27); David Pingree, Picatrix: The Latin Version of the \u288 ?\u257 \'e2yat al-\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u7717 ?\plain \f2\fs26 ak\u299 \'eem, London 1986 (Studies of the Warburg Institute, Bd. 39), S. xii \endash  x\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 v, xx \endash  lvii, bes. S. xvi (Class I, Sigle D)\plain \f2\fs26 ; Jean-Patrice Boudet/ Jean Charles Coulon, La version Arabe (Gh\u257 \'e2yat al-\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u7717 ?\plain \f2\fs26 ak\u299 \'eem) et la version Latine du Picatrix. Pointes communs et divergences, in: Jean-Patrice-Boudet/ Isabelle Draelants (Hrsg.), Textes et savo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 irs scientifiques et magiques m\u233 \'e9di\u233 \'e9vaux entre Orient et Occident, Paris 2017 (CRMH. Cahiers de recherches m\u233 \'e9di\u233 \'e9vales et humanistes. A Journal of Medieval and Humanistic Studies 33 (2017)), S. 67 \endash  101; vgl. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Thorndike/ Kibre 1963, Sp. 52}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; Thorndike, History, 1923 \endash  1958, Bd. 2 (1923), S. 813 \endash  824; Reimund Leicht, Astrologumena Judaica, Untersuchungen zur Geschichte der astrologischen Literatur der Juden, T\u252 \'fcbingen 2006 (Texts and Studies in Medieval and Early Modern Judaism, Bd. 21), S. 316 \endash  320; Text auch in {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5007[0].501m/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Hs 1410}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , 88\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [1+\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ],  \endash  IV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r/v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  leer.}

