\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 143\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  145\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6922/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Tabulae}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ad inveniendum locum Solis. (143\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tabula prima ad inveniendum locum Solis in anno bisextili cum motu octave spere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <; (144\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tabula secunda ad inveniendum locum Solis in anno primo post bisextum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <; (144\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tabula tercia ad inveniendum locum Solis in anno secundo post bisextum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <; (145\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tabula quarta ad inveniendum locum Solis in anno tercio post bisextum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <; (145\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tabula utriusque declinacionis Solis ab equinocte vel equatore die\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < mit Expositio:{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17  In hac tabula habetur per quot horas naturales Sol in quolibet signorum in ascensu suo moratur}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hec contratabula Solis ostendit eius declinacionis die mensis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 in omnium climate est agendum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .}

