\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  58\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 John Mandeville}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Itinerarius a terra Angliae in partes Hierosolomitanas}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit ytinerarius a terra Anglie in partes Yerosolomitanas et in ulteriores transmarinas editus primo in lingwa Gallicorum a milite suo auctore anno incarnacionis domini m\u176 \'b0 ccc\u176 \'b0 lv in civitate Leodiensi et paulo post in eadem civitate translatus in hanc formam literam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Commendacio brevis terre Jherosolomitate capitulum primum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Cum terra Jhersolomitana promissionis filiorum dei dignior cunctis}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (58\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 hic itaque finis sit scripti de quo deus gloriosus una ad toto curia celestis cetum nunc ac eius temporibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 In seculorum secula sit benedictus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et sic est finis presentis itinerarij dictus Mandevil continens in se raras ac delectabiles materias. Collectum in Embek a reverendissimo baculario Bertoldo de Paderborne per me Iohannem Tremonie in vigilia Nativitatis beate Marie virginis infra horam primam et secundam sub anno domini m\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  cccc\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  lix\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (7. September 1459). \endash  Wohl Text der Vulgata-Version; Druck: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 GW M20392, M20393, M20395, M20386, M20399, M20401, M20403, M20405}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; vgl. Johann Vogels, Die ungedruckten lateini\-schen Versionen Mandeville\rquote s, in: M. Wollseiffen (Hrsg.), Programm des Gymnasi\-ums zu Crefeld Nr. 397. Schuljahr IX. Von Ostern 1885 bis Ostern 1886, Krefeld 1886, S. 3 \endash  23; Josephine Waters Bennett, The Rediscovery of Sir John Mandeville, New York 1954 (The Modern Language Association of America. Monograph Series, Bd. 19), S. 298 \endash  310; VL(2), Bd. 5 (1985), Sp. 1201 \endash  1214 (Ernst Bremer); Little, Initia, 1904 (1958), S. 61. \endash  58\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  59\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  leer; 59\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Besitzvermerk s.o. Geschichte.}

