\pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb600\sa360\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 230\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  235\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Albertus Magnus}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Speculum Astronomiae}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (230\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rab\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Rubrik: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit Speculum Astronomie domini Alberti Magni Ratisponensis episcopi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (230\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Prolog: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Occassione quorundam librorum, apud quos non est radix sciencie}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... Kapitel 1: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Due magne sapiencie sunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (235\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sed quia ambo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 inveniuntur ab eodem causata\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et sic est finis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: Stefano Caroti u.a. (Hrsg.), Alberto Magno. Speculum Astronomiae, 1977 (s. Lit.), S. 5 \endash  48; Paola Zambelli, The Speculum Astronomiae And Its Enigma: Astrology, Theology And Science in Albertus Magnus And Its Contemporaries, Dordrecht 1992 (Boston Studies in the Philosophy of Science, Bd. 135), S. 208 \endash  272; zur Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung vgl. ebenda, S. 203 \endash  205 (Hs. erw\u228 \'e4hnt S. 205); Caroti (s.o.), S. 118 \endash  120; Glorieux, R\u233 \'e9pertoire, S. 62 \endash  77, Nr. 6dj.), 193c.) (unter Philippe de Thory), 312br.) (unter Roger Bacon); ders., Facult\u233 \'e9, S. 77, Nr. 14dj.); Mohan, Initia, 1975 \endash  1978, (1977), S. 261*; Lynn Thorndike, Traditional Medieval Tracts Concerning Engraved Astrological Images, in: M\u233 \'e9langes Auguste Pelzer. \plain \f2\lang1024\fs26 \u201 \'c9tudes \u271 \'ef histoire litt\u233 \'e9raire et doctrinale de la scolastique m\u233 \'e9di\u233 \'e9vale offertes \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u224 \'e0 Mgr Auguste Pelzer, scriptor de la biblioth\u232 \'e8que Vaticane, \u224 \'e0 l'occasion de son soixante-dixi\u232 \'e8me anniversaire, Leuven 1947 (Universit\u233 \'e9 de Louvain. Recueil de travaux d'histoire et de philologie, 3e s\u233 \'e9rie, 26e fascicule), S. 217 \endash  274, bes. S. 217 \endash  221; Agostino Paravicini Bagliani, Le Speculum Astronomiae, une \u233 \'e9nigme? Enqu\u234 \'eate sur les manuscrits, Turnhout 2001 (Micrologus\lquote  Library, Bd. 6), S. 4 \endash  5, 18, 46 \endash  48, 59, 79, 92, fig. 4 (234\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 /235\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ); C.A.L.M.A., Bd. 1,2 (2000), S. 121 \endash  132 (Lidia Lanza). \endash  235\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  236\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  leer. }

